{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, for reasons of its bulk, mass, size, design, and siting would be detrimental to the character of the plot and wider area, closing off the openness of the corner plot to the rear and side and&amp;nbsp;and failing to reflect the prevelant roof design in the area,&amp;nbsp;therefore failing to integrate with the existing character of the area and design of the dwellings whilst also failing to preserve the historic fabric of the Becontree Estate. It is also considered to result in an unacceptable loss of private amenity space which is at odds with the character and appearance of the area. The proposal is therefore considered to overdevelop the plot. The proposed dwelling is therefore deemed to be unacceptable and contrary to:Paragraphs&amp;nbsp; 131, 135 and 203 of the National Planning Policy Framework (DLUHC, September 2023)Policies D1, D4, and HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy CP3 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010)Policies BP8 and BP11 of the Local Development Framework (LDF)Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Policies SP2, Part 6 of SPP6, DMD1, and DMD6 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan 2037 (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)",
    "The proposed development fails to provide sufficient external amenity space to facilitate a good quality of life.&nbsp; As such, the proposed development is considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:Part F(9) in Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy BP5&nbsp;ocal Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Part 6 in Policy DMNE1&nbsp;&nbsp;of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan 2037&nbsp;(Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021).",
    "The&nbsp;proposed development, for reasons of its&nbsp;bulk, mass and size, would result in a significant loss of daylight and outlook,&nbsp;whilst also resulting in unacceptable levels of&nbsp;overshadowing and would be very overbearing for neighbouring dwellings especially no.99 Fitzstephen Road (the existing dwelling). The proposal would therefore have an unneighbourly impact and&nbsp;is therefore considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:Paragraph 130(f) of the National Planning Policy Framework (DLUHC, September 2023)Policy D6&nbsp;of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy CP3 of Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010)Policies BP5, BP8, and BP11 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD6 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan 2037&nbsp;(Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)"
  ],
